  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 337 PM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nSurface high pressure will slide eastward this weekend into early \nnext week. This will keep conditions below normal with lows in the \n20s and highs in the 40s through this weekend along with more than \nample sunshine. As the high slides to the east of the area next \nweek, return flow will allow for temperatures to gradually rise \ntoward climatological values for mid-November. Mid-levels in this \nextended period will be largely dominated by a ridge of high \npressure until mid to late next week. Outside of a shortwave trough \nscooting south of the area late this weekend and early next week \nwith any moisture well south of the area, the next chance for rain \nwill be late next week, perhaps later. Toward midweek is when a lead \nshortwave trough will be lifting northeastward toward the region and \ncould offer the first chance for rain, though this may wait until a \ntrailing trough digs and sprawls over the Southwest by the following \nweekend.",
